---
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import Code from '../components/Code.astro';
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const checkout = `git clone https://github.com/wesflo/lockxy.git
cd lockxy
pnpm install`;

const startBoth = `pnpm dev`;

const demoCommands = `# Standard manifest and the complete fixture set
pnpm --filter @wesflo/lockxy-demo dev

# No mock.manifest.json: naming conventions must keep working
pnpm dev:missing-manifest

# Malformed mock.manifest.json: expose the error and preserve file fallback
pnpm dev:invalid-manifest`;

const playgroundCommands = `# Start only the plugin + panel integration
pnpm dev:playground

# Optionally pass bypassed requests to a real development API
PLAYGROUND_API_TARGET=https://dev-api.example.com pnpm dev:playground`;

const checks = `# Vite plugin unit tests
pnpm test:package

# Demo tests
pnpm test:app

# Proxy panel unit tests
pnpm --filter @wesflo/lockxy-panel test

# Build the complete workspace
pnpm build`;
---

<DocsLayout
    title="Local verification"
    description="Use the Lockxy demo and playground to verify the Vite plugin and proxy panel locally."
    activePath="/local-verification/"
>
    <article>
        <p class="kicker">Work on Lockxy</p>
        <h1>Verify each layer in isolation.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
            The repository contains two browser applications with deliberately different responsibilities. Use the demo
            to inspect the Vite plugin by itself, then use the playground when the proxy panel must participate.
        </p>

        <h2 id="checkout-and-start">Checkout and start</h2>
        <p>The workspace expects Node.js 24 and pnpm 11.</p>
        <Code code={checkout} label="terminal" />
        <p>Start both verification applications from the repository root:</p>
        <Code code={startBoth} label="terminal" />
        <ul>
            <li><a href="http://localhost:5173"><code>http://localhost:5173</code></a> — standalone plugin demo</li>
            <li><a href="http://localhost:5174"><code>http://localhost:5174</code></a> — plugin and panel playground</li>
        </ul>
        <Callout title="Start with the smallest surface">
            <p>
                Reproduce resolver, response, or manifest problems in the demo first. If the demo behaves correctly but
                the playground does not, the remaining investigation can focus on panel state, cookies, and local storage.
            </p>
        </Callout>

        <h2 id="plugin-demo">Plugin demo</h2>
        <p>
            The demo exercises <code>@wesflo/vite-plugin-lockxy</code> without importing or mounting
            <code>@wesflo/lockxy-panel</code>. Its browser interface is only a request harness: it sends the same calls
            an application would send and displays status, headers, timing, and response content.
        </p>
        <p>Use the standard demo to verify:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>method-specific and generic naming-convention precedence;</li>
            <li>shorter-path fallback when a more specific file is absent;</li>
            <li>JSON, text, binary PDF, and empty responses;</li>
            <li>HTTP errors and bodyless <code>204</code> responses;</li>
            <li>fixed and random delays;</li>
            <li>explicit files, endpoint defaults, and automatically applied single scenarios.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="demo-modes">Demo modes</h2>
        <Code code={demoCommands} label="terminal" />
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr><th>Mode</th><th>Mock root</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>dev</code></td>
                    <td><code>apps/demo/mock/</code></td>
                    <td>Exercises the complete fixture set and a valid manifest.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>dev:missing-manifest</code></td>
                    <td><code>apps/demo/mock-missing/</code></td>
                    <td>
                        Proves that <code>mock.manifest.json</code> is optional and convention-only requests remain plug and
                        play. A manifest error in the demo UI is expected; run the manifest-fallback request to verify the
                        mock response itself.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>dev:invalid-manifest</code></td>
                    <td><code>apps/demo/mock-invalid/</code></td>
                    <td>
                        Makes the manifest route report malformed JSON while a naming-convention fixture remains available.
                        This separates manifest error reporting from the file resolver fallback.
                    </td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>
            These package scripts first run <code>cleanViteCache</code>, which removes only the demo's generated
            <code>node_modules/.vite</code> pre-bundle cache. That guarantees a fresh Vite start while the linked workspace
            plugin and its modes are being changed; it does not remove dependencies, mock files, or project state.
        </p>

        <h2 id="proxy-playground">Proxy playground</h2>
        <p>
            The playground loads the same kinds of requests and fixtures, but also mounts the real
            <code>&lt;wf-lockxy-panel&gt;</code> Web Component. Use it to verify the integration between the panel, its
            browser persistence, and the Vite middleware.
        </p>
        <Code code={playgroundCommands} label="terminal" />
        <p>A useful manual check is:</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Select a request and run it once to establish the default response.</li>
            <li>Open the floating panel and choose another scenario for that endpoint.</li>
            <li>Run the request again and compare status, delay, and response body.</li>
            <li>Disable only that endpoint and confirm it is passed to the next Vite middleware.</li>
            <li>Disable the proxy globally and confirm that every matching request is passed through.</li>
            <li>Reload the page to verify the enabled-on-load and optional selection persistence settings.</li>
            <li>Use <strong>Reset all settings</strong> and confirm that panel cookies and local-storage state are removed.</li>
        </ol>
        <Callout title="Testing a real development API">
            <p>
                Set <code>PLAYGROUND_API_TARGET</code> to configure the playground's Vite proxy. Requests bypassed by the
                panel can then continue to that API. Without a target, a bypass normally ends in Vite's fallback response;
                that still proves the mock middleware did not handle it.
            </p>
        </Callout>

        <h2 id="what-to-run">What to run</h2>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr><th>Question</th><th>Best verification surface</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td>Does a URL resolve to the correct local file?</td><td>Standard demo</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Does the plugin work without a manifest?</td><td>Missing-manifest demo mode</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Is an invalid manifest reported without breaking convention fallback?</td><td>Invalid-manifest demo mode</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Does a status, delay, file, or single scenario apply correctly?</td><td>Standard demo</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Does changing a scenario in the browser affect the next request?</td><td>Playground</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Do endpoint and global bypass reach a development API?</td><td>Playground with an API target</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Are panel selections, startup state, and launcher position restored?</td><td>Playground</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2 id="repository-map">Repository map</h2>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr><th>Path</th><th>What to find there</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>packages/vite-plugin-lockxy/</code></td><td>Vite middleware, manifest handling, resolver logic, and plugin tests.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>packages/lockxy-panel/</code></td><td>Embeddable proxy panel, browser state, cookies, and panel tests.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>packages/local-mock-api-ui/</code></td><td>Shared UI elements used by the repository applications and panel.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>packages/local-mock-api-utils/</code></td><td>Shared browser and protocol utilities.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>apps/demo/</code></td><td>Plugin-only browser harness, its modes, fixtures, and request cases.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>apps/playground/</code></td><td>Plugin-and-panel integration harness with matching request fixtures.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2 id="automated-checks">Automated checks</h2>
        <p>After reproducing behavior in the appropriate browser application, run the focused tests and final build:</p>
        <Code code={checks} label="terminal" />
    </article>
</DocsLayout>
